    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay got it. i'll check the rating on the side. one more thing, i've noticed sometimes the noise just totally disappears for an hour and then comes back even though i haven't touched anything. it's like it's just acting up for no reason. why would it be so intermittent like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Intermittent humming often means the capacitor is failing “softly”—it can hold enough charge to start the motor sporadically, then lose its ability as it heats up. Another common culprit is a loose or corroded connection on the fan motor or capacitor that makes contact only when vibrations shift the contacts. A failing fan motor bearing can also temporarily seize and then release as it warms up. Check all terminals for tightness, clean any corrosion, and replace the capacitor; if the problem persists, the motor itself likely needs professional diagnosis.",
      "source": "target",
